<!--Post: 6273--><!--Time: 1107647591-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6273"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Researcher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Researcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 3:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->An Open Letter To BTK from the Internet Community <BR> <BR>Title is to be kept as is. To be copied and signed by nick and posted on every BTK Internet site. Simple copy/paste and add your nick to the original message and keep the post growing. <BR> <BR> <BR>BTK, <BR> <BR>In all of your communications with the media and the WPD you reference messages  that cannot be passed on to the public due to the ongoing investigation into your activities. <BR> <BR>As you know you have been receiving publicity not just from the local Wichita media, but also from national media.  But what about the Internet community? <BR> <BR>There is a large group of people interested in the BTK case for various reasons. Many are in the Wichita area as well as the United States and overseas. Some use <BR>blogs, web pages and discussion boards to study the case. <BR> <BR>We the undersigned ask you to address us directly in your next communication with whatever you want to say. What is your message to us? <BR> <BR>Specifically, we ask that you request that KAKE pass your message on to us through the media - something that will not have to be filtered through the WPD.   <BR> <BR>I sign my name first as the originator of this message to you. <BR> <BR>We await your reply. <BR> <BR>Investigator <BR>Sardonicus <BR>thekota <BR>researcher<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6273-->
<!--Post: 6276--><!--Time: 1107648536-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6276"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lorenap<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lorenap<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 4:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->DITTO! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6276-->
<!--Post: 6291--><!--Time: 1107661639-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6291"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 7:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->OK. I am all for challenging BTK. To get help, to turn himself in. To give us valuable information that would help the families or justice.  <BR>To ask him to copy us on his next &#34;communication&#34; because we feel left out is, with all due respect, WAY, WAY, WAY beyond the pale. Just my opinion, but I cannot support this one. Sorry. If it served some pubic good or served a helpful purpose, it would be one thing. I fail to see how this does that <i>at all</i>, even a little bit.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6291-->
<!--Post: 6296--><!--Time: 1107663102-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6296"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 8:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK won&#39;t ever do what someone asks or requests he do. He must be in charge. Study the next drop  carefully and maybe you&#39;ll see a little wink to something on the boards, but it&#39;ll be on BTK&#39;s terms. Control. I agree with Dpinva, and as Tom wrote a while back: <i>&#34;BTK&#39;s done his own thing for 30 years and I doubt he can be manipulated.&#34;</i> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6296-->
<!--Post: 6319--><!--Time: 1107677997-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6319"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 12:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He can&#39;t control the Monster. I guess it&#39;s true: Everyone has a Boss. <BR> <BR>Researcher is correct though. BTK is being very inefficient in dispersing his information through the media and the police exclusively. They both have alterior agendas. The BTK case makes a great excuse for cost overruns and &#39;secret case files&#39; in the department. To the Media: BTK case=Advertizing$ &#40;as long as it keeps people interested&#41;. Either way, neither group has any incentive to do anything other than say &#34;There is a serial killer at large and we are staying right on top of events as they unfold. Pay attention to us and don&#39;t ask questions and we will take care of it&#34;. It&#39;s a formula that&#39;s served them well for thirty years. <BR> <BR>&#40;do you suppose that if the mayor get&#39;s a traffic ticket he calls the chief and asks &#34;can you put this in the BTK file?&#34;.&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6319-->
